# ── Allowlist: ignore everything, re-admit what belongs ──
*
!*/

!*.py
!*.docx
!*.configuration

# Build-critical: not .py/.docx, but CI cannot run without them
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!pytest.ini
!requirements.txt
!requirements-dev.txt
!*.yml
!*.yaml
!*.config
# Root-level markdown: ReadMe.md and HANDOVER.md are both documents the
# repo cannot be understood without. A pattern rather than another
# exact-name rule, because this allowlist has now silently swallowed
# three files (mc_history.json, archive/README.md, HANDOVER.md).
!/*.md
!docs/*.md

# archive/ holds superseded code kept ON PURPOSE, each file carrying
# its own provenance. Distinct from older_versions/ below, which is
# deliberately untracked. The .py files come in via !*.py above.
!archive/*.md

# Golden baseline
!tests/golden/snapshots/*.csv

!ruff.toml
!tests/golden/fixtures/
!tests/golden/fixtures/*.json

# Denied regardless of the above — last match wins
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.bak
older_versions/
allocate_funds_v0.9.py
test/portfolio_allocator.py
.idea/
.venv/

# project_to_md.py — generated bundle output
Code packaged into MDs for LLMs/
# Added by code-review-graph
.code-review-graph/

# AI assistant instruction files — local to each machine, not shared.
# Root-level .md is admitted by `!/*.md` above for HANDOVER.md, so these
# need explicit denies here, after it. Last match wins.
/AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
/CODEBUDDY.md
/GEMINI.md
/QODER.md

# Schema DDL is source, not data. The ignore rule above is for dumps
# and backups; it swallowed db/ratings_schema.sql silently once.
!db/*.sql
